## Architecture

This app is built on the [platform-infra](https://github.com/{{ github_handle }}/platform-infra) stack.

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Backend | FastAPI (Python 3.13), served via DigitalOcean App Platform |
| Database | PostgreSQL 18 on a shared managed cluster (private VPC) |
| Cache / Queue | Valkey 8 on a shared managed instance (Redis-compatible; DO replaced Managed Redis with Valkey in mid-2025) |
{% if include_frontend -%}
| Frontend | Next.js (TypeScript), deployed to DigitalOcean App Platform |
{% endif -%}
{% if include_ios -%}
| iOS | SwiftUI |
{% endif -%}
| Infrastructure | Pulumi (Python), stack `{{ pulumi_org }}/{{ app_name }}/prod` |
| Auth | Clerk |
| Feature Flags | Flagsmith |
| Error Tracking | Sentry |
| Observability | Honeycomb |

## Local Development

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.13+, [`uv`](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)
{% if include_frontend -%}
- Node.js 24+
{% endif -%}
- Docker (for local Postgres + Valkey)

### Backend

```bash
# Create the git-ignored env files (backend/.env{% if include_frontend %}, frontend/.env.local{% endif %}) and fill
# the SaaS dev keys from Pulumi config without echoing them. Every key is
# optional; without one, that integration degrades gracefully. DATABASE_URL and
# REDIS_URL point at docker compose, never the shared cluster.
bash scripts/dev-env.sh        # or: cp backend/.env.example backend/.env

# Start local Postgres + Valkey
docker compose up -d --wait

# Install dependencies and run
cd backend
uv sync
uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

The API is at http://localhost:8000. Routes answer both with and without the
`/api` prefix (production serves them under `/api`), e.g.
http://localhost:8000/api/health and http://localhost:8000/api/docs.
`/me` and `/notes` return 401 without a Clerk session token.
{% if include_frontend %}

### Frontend

```bash
cd frontend
cp -n .env.example .env.local   # already created if you ran scripts/dev-env.sh
npm install
npm run dev
```

The frontend is at http://localhost:3000 and calls the backend at
`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` (http://localhost:8000; CORS allows `localhost:3000`
via `CORS_ORIGINS`). Without `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` it shows a
setup notice. `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are inlined when the dev server starts, so
restart `npm run dev` after changing `.env.local`.
{% endif %}

