## Environment Variables

See `backend/.env.example`{% if include_frontend %}, `frontend/.env.example`,{% endif %} and the root
`.env.example` reference for required variables and documentation. In production,
these are injected by Pulumi as App Platform secrets — you never manage them manually.

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | PostgreSQL connection string (asyncpg driver) |
| `REDIS_URL` | Redis connection URL |
| `DEBUG` | Enable debug mode (default: `false`) |
| `ENVIRONMENT` | Runtime environment (`development` / `production`) |
{% if include_frontend -%}
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` | Backend API URL for the frontend |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` | Clerk publishable key for the frontend |
{% endif -%}
| `CLERK_SECRET_KEY` | Clerk authentication secret |
| `FLAGSMITH_API_KEY` | Flagsmith server-side environment key |
| `SENTRY_DSN` | Sentry DSN for error reporting |
| `HONEYCOMB_API_KEY` | Honeycomb ingest key for observability |

## Deploying to the shared platform

The full first-time procedure, including which key to copy from each vendor, is
the [platform-app-template README](https://github.com/{{ github_handle }}/platform-app-template#usage).
In short, from the repo root:

```bash
# DigitalOcean token for local Pulumi runs (app-deployer, issued by your admin)
export DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN="$(cat ~/.config/platform/app-deployer.token)"

bash scripts/preflight-new-app.sh      # checks GitHub, Pulumi, DO token, secrets

cd infra
pulumi stack init prod                 # first time only; you own this stack
# Copy each value in the vendor UI, then run its line (keeps it out of history):
pbpaste | pulumi config set --secret clerk_secret_key
pbpaste | pulumi config set --secret flagsmith_api_key   # server-side key, ser.…
pbpaste | pulumi config set --secret sentry_dsn
pbpaste | pulumi config set --secret honeycomb_api_key   # ingest key, 64 chars
{%- if include_frontend %}
pbpaste | pulumi config set clerk_publishable_key        # pk_test_…, not secret
{%- endif %}
git add Pulumi.prod.yaml && git commit -m "chore: prod config" && git push   # CI reads it (values are encrypted)

pulumi up                              # creates the app + per-app database/user/pool
```

The app comes up with `/api/health` reporting `"database": "waiting"` until the
platform admin onboards it (one time, in platform-infra:
`./scripts/onboard-app.sh {{ app_name }}`). After onboarding the app connects on
its own within about a minute; no redeploy is needed. Then:

```bash
bash scripts/verify-live.sh            # passes once "database" is "ready"
```

After that, every merge to `main` deploys automatically (GitHub Actions runs
`pulumi up`; App Platform rebuilds on push).

## Credentials reference

| Credential | Where it lives | Who provides it |
|---|---|---|
| `DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN` (`app-deployer`) | local env + GitHub Actions secret | you (issued by admin) |
| `PULUMI_ACCESS_TOKEN` | local + GitHub Actions secret | you |
| `clerk_secret_key` | Pulumi config secret | you (Clerk **Development** instance) |
| `clerk_publishable_key` | Pulumi config (non-secret) | you (frontend only) |
| `flagsmith_api_key` | Pulumi config secret | you (server-side environment key) |
| `sentry_dsn` | Pulumi config secret | you |
| `honeycomb_api_key` | Pulumi config secret | you (ingest key) |
| Trusted source + schema grant | platform clusters | **platform admin** (onboard-app.sh) |

## GitHub Actions Secrets Required

| Secret | Description |
|---|---|
| `PULUMI_ACCESS_TOKEN` | Pulumi Cloud token (used by deploy workflow) |
| `DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN` | `app-deployer` DigitalOcean token (used by deploy workflow) |

Set each by copying it, then `pbpaste | gh secret set <NAME>`. Until both exist,
the deploy workflow skips with a warning. SaaS credentials are **Pulumi config
secrets**, not GitHub secrets; Pulumi injects them into App Platform at deploy.

## Tearing it down

`pulumi destroy` needs `database:delete`, which the `app-deployer` token
deliberately lacks, so ask the platform admin to run it with their token. Then
remove the app's ID from platform-infra `trusted_app_ids` (PR), delete the
GitHub repo, and delete the Clerk app, Flagsmith key, Sentry project and
Honeycomb key.

## Feature Flags

Feature flags are managed in [Flagsmith](https://flagsmith.com). To add a flag:

1. Create the flag in the Flagsmith dashboard. On the free plan all apps share
   one project, so prefix it with the app name (e.g. `{{ app_name | replace('-', '_') }}_my_feature`).
2. Read it in Python (see `backend/app/api/feature.py`):
   ```python
   from flagsmith import Flagsmith
   flagsmith = Flagsmith(environment_key=settings.flagsmith_api_key)
   is_enabled = flagsmith.get_environment_flags().is_feature_enabled("{{ app_name | replace('-', '_') }}_my_feature")
   ```

